values ('e7f8a9b0-1c2d-4e57-8f67-7a8b9c0d1e97', 'political-parties-and-elections', 'Political Parties and Elections', 'Students learn why parties and elections are the central linkage institutions between citizens, interests, candidates, governments, and policy. The course covers party theories and party systems, the U.S. two-party system, realignment, and dealignment, party organization and nominations, political socialization and voting behavior, polling and election data, campaign strategy and mobilization, media and digital campaigning, campaign finance and interest groups, primaries and intraparty conflict, general elections and the Electoral College, election administration and voting rights, polarization and democratic accountability, comparative electoral systems, and data-driven election analysis.');

