  'Political Parties and Elections',
  'Students learn why parties and elections are the central linkage institutions between citizens, interests, candidates, governments, and policy. The course covers party theories and party systems, the U.S. two-party system, realignment, and dealignment, party organization and nominations, political socialization and voting behavior, polling and election data, campaign strategy and mobilization, media and digital campaigning, campaign finance and interest groups, primaries and intraparty conflict, general elections and the Electoral College, election administration and voting rights, polarization and democratic accountability, comparative electoral systems, and data-driven election analysis.',
  $ppeljson${"slug": "political-parties-and-elections", "title": "Political Parties and Elections", "description": "Students learn why parties and elections are the central linkage institutions between citizens, interests, candidates, governments, and policy. The course covers party theories and party systems, the U.S. two-party system, realignment, and dealignment, party organization and nominations, political socialization and voting behavior, polling and election data, campaign strategy and mobilization, media and digital campaigning, campaign finance and interest groups, primaries and intraparty conflict, general elections and the Electoral College, election administration and voting rights, polarization and democratic accountability, comparative electoral systems, and data-driven election analysis.", "topics": [{"id": "18fdc29f-98ef-4aa2-91e4-7287d7b25adb", "type": "topic", "title": "The Study of Parties, Elections, and Democratic Representation", "description": "Students learn why parties and elections are the central linkage institutions between citizens, interests, candidates, governments, and policy.", "children": [{"id": "cc4b398c-fe9c-47a7-828c-f0f3ec62f6ae", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Linkage institutions", "children": [{"id": "2caf5d49-e00a-479c-9e3a-008517542ff5", "type": "concept", "title": "Representation and accountability"}, {"id": "664bf605-338d-4dcc-b729-c43e13395f6e", "type": "concept", "title": "Aggregation of interests"}, {"id": "d44d6347-17e7-4ba0-979e-b6435b59e605", "type": "concept", "title": "Recruitment and coordination"}], "description": "Parties and elections connect public preferences to governing authority."}, {"id": "ff448c5f-978e-432c-9523-531286ba7044", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Core questions", "children": [{"id": "6f8388b3-5898-468e-9cfb-249cd1d7b24c", "type": "concept", "title": "Why do party systems differ?"}, {"id": "393fe12a-5af3-4027-b142-c3bdd64702ce", "type": "concept", "title": "Why do people vote as they do?"}, {"id": "c811ac78-9601-45d2-b060-13bd5a32435d", "type": "concept", "title": "Do elections produce responsive government?"}], "description": "Students learn the big puzzles that organize the course."}, {"id": "ee08ac82-7e0f-4821-bbdb-31a96286addc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Evidence and methods", "children": [{"id": "dd8d7f81-2cf9-4cac-b1b2-7002bf39f700", "type": "concept", "title": "Survey data"}, {"id": "aaaca492-5fba-4cf7-a42f-de013df70d15", "type": "concept", "title": "Election returns"}, {"id": "5c1cd324-fba2-4dab-9a83-34d250763116", "type": "concept", "title": "Campaign finance and media data"}], "description": "Election analysis depends on data and institutional detail."}]}, {"id": "0c94d062-df17-42e9-81d2-099a0dfec256", "type": "topic", "title": "Theories of Political Parties and Party Systems", "description": "This topic explains what parties are, why they form, and how party systems structure democratic competition.", "children": [{"id": "448c0819-aaaa-442e-9adb-868368b3f31f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "What parties do", "children": [{"id": "e2a572c4-3a0f-4ce3-a8b3-f208f4a0231c", "type": "concept", "title": "Nomination and recruitment"}, {"id": "f01644c9-009c-4e8f-9fec-e57db6e76bb9", "type": "concept", "title": "Branding and voter cues"}, {"id": "a597d124-cd16-4e23-a1a2-688ef9d3de80", "type": "concept", "title": "Legislative organization"}], "description": "Parties are teams that solve coordination problems in elections and government."}, {"id": "4d4f9650-301a-43f8-a2c5-6ed636e85798", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Party system theories", "children": [{"id": "a59acdcf-2f28-4400-b9c7-647b3741d24d", "type": "concept", "title": "Duverger's law"}, {"id": "073a9042-fe7d-45ac-8925-99046600959e", "type": "concept", "title": "Cleavages and social bases"}, {"id": "71bd64fd-956c-4f9d-99d7-02032772c7c9", "type": "concept", "title": "Party system institutionalization"}], "description": "Institutions shape how many parties can compete effectively."}, {"id": "9deedb53-9737-4003-a37b-dc25952d1d99", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Party change", "children": [{"id": "803a66d9-c0e7-4e22-a894-684144363d4f", "type": "concept", "title": "Issue evolution"}, {"id": "ee746125-48c7-4c96-95b2-0be8f59ea621", "type": "concept", "title": "Coalition maintenance"}, {"id": "2aa90958-d0b9-4e22-b23f-38acc7f33aa9", "type": "concept", "title": "New parties and party decline"}], "description": "Parties adapt to voters, elites, rules, and crises."}]}, {"id": "1b6cafe1-745a-44d6-88d5-553811a9cd01", "type": "topic", "title": "The U.S. Two-Party System, Realignment, and Dealignment", "description": "Students examine why the United States has a durable two-party system and how coalitions change over time.", "children": [{"id": "d7588116-f999-4d03-b56c-9bffd2bc16c4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Two-party durability", "children": [{"id": "8a1e875b-758b-4413-b768-349376d4e72e", "type": "concept", "title": "Single-member districts"}, {"id": "2979bd38-2e9d-472c-bccf-17f0c78631b0", "type": "concept", "title": "Plurality rules"}, {"id": "9a30d580-7551-49d7-bb46-fa74f01b25cc", "type": "concept", "title": "Ballot access and federalism"}], "description": "Students learn why U.S. institutions favor two major parties."}, {"id": "23930437-4432-4bc2-b00a-5a7c8ceacdcb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Realignment", "children": [{"id": "c4578772-8fac-4f20-867c-472c6fcb66fc", "type": "concept", "title": "Critical elections"}, {"id": "abf09b97-09fa-41bd-ba92-58f875bf7a3e", "type": "concept", "title": "New Deal coalition"}, {"id": "a07e02b6-05a0-41e2-b406-36842f88580f", "type": "concept", "title": "Southern realignment"}], "description": "Party coalitions can shift around major issues and crises."}, {"id": "62f23da4-d00b-44b0-bde4-3d32c15e465d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Dealignment and sorting", "children": [{"id": "8e165019-de2d-49b2-84e4-0e8b8c7c500b", "type": "concept", "title": "Independent identifiers"}, {"id": "9b66a2f2-02ae-4fb5-89d7-d7a28fec0f84", "type": "concept", "title": "Negative partisanship"}, {"id": "4b8f5f60-ebae-4ec7-b170-80547de05d07", "type": "concept", "title": "Ideological consistency"}], "description": "Voters may weaken old ties while becoming more ideologically sorted."}]}, {"id": "07c1613c-2e2e-4bbc-91ca-37f66451a603", "type": "topic", "title": "Party Organization, Activists, Elites, and Nominations", "description": "This module studies parties as organizations made of voters, activists, donors, interest groups, officeholders, and campaign professionals.", "children": [{"id": "6705c197-32ba-4ed6-b9e3-d81f9204e04f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Formal organizations", "children": [{"id": "0008d293-2d8b-4877-a908-e8b2c4bd8ac7", "type": "concept", "title": "National committees"}, {"id": "026c013f-3f21-492c-afa3-139e1bae2cbc", "type": "concept", "title": "State and local parties"}, {"id": "a21e459e-af98-4d66-be67-cc8fd3e81876", "type": "concept", "title": "Campaign committees"}], "description": "Parties have national, state, local, and congressional structures."}, {"id": "8f37404b-80be-4698-8e89-dc13f72100b8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Activists and elites", "children": [{"id": "5d02cb03-b27d-409c-a9bd-33041b54cf14", "type": "concept", "title": "Party activists"}, {"id": "16b04dfb-401c-4b52-819b-b3b8f569d69e", "type": "concept", "title": "Donors and interest groups"}, {"id": "4159dada-97d5-47f0-b119-74523edaec6d", "type": "concept", "title": "Endorsements and invisible primaries"}], "description": "High-engagement actors often shape nominations and agendas."}, {"id": "67cb0d0b-2237-4ec0-8df5-423c49bf956d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Party networks", "children": [{"id": "96876768-e431-4f27-ba6f-3943e590f7f3", "type": "concept", "title": "Consultants and data vendors"}, {"id": "c26d0780-3d82-4365-8797-2baa385f4eed", "type": "concept", "title": "Advocacy groups"}, {"id": "60fb8c38-6a19-44fb-88bf-7bfe5947d4ac", "type": "concept", "title": "Media and aligned organizations"}], "description": "Modern parties are networks as much as formal institutions."}]}, {"id": "85f98bba-9fa0-4e09-b6b1-fcea13eca058", "type": "topic", "title": "Political Socialization, Party Identification, and Voting Behavior", "description": "Students learn how voters form political attachments and make electoral choices.", "children": [{"id": "102794d4-fa4f-430a-bea5-7ff0279bf582", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Party identification", "children": [{"id": "ed46325a-7aea-48c9-8916-dd7d9f040a04", "type": "concept", "title": "The Michigan model"}, {"id": "9695171a-aad2-43bf-845f-83accd9f5850", "type": "concept", "title": "Social identity and affect"}, {"id": "9ef71c3b-0e0d-46f9-8127-2d278359725c", "type": "concept", "title": "Retrospective and prospective voting"}], "description": "Partisanship is a long-term attachment that structures perception and choice."}, {"id": "b700e3d1-560b-454f-bfc3-7f127985409a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Social cleavages", "children": [{"id": "16a1db13-b980-45b6-b285-cfa1e0cccdc6", "type": "concept", "title": "Class, race, religion, gender, age, education, geography"}, {"id": "e5d94170-5da0-4278-8807-171cc31547df", "type": "concept", "title": "Urban-rural divides"}, {"id": "f954d2f5-4dee-437f-b72b-a39175a56185", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethnicity and immigration"}], "description": "Voting patterns reflect social location and group identities."}, {"id": "a96e6204-cc74-4ee4-a22c-1aa399e888ef", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Turnout and participation", "children": [{"id": "b7f08729-5a5a-450f-a9ad-6440d92d4b41", "type": "concept", "title": "Civic skills and resources"}, {"id": "ad57ed9e-135b-4e8b-994b-f9f5a05bc3ba", "type": "concept", "title": "Mobilization and social pressure"}, {"id": "fd53b1b2-1737-4180-a293-b731dc702589", "type": "concept", "title": "Costs of voting"}], "description": "Voting is shaped by resources, motivation, mobilization, and rules."}]}, {"id": "243a8cf4-4b6e-422b-b7e5-1bf49a21ca00", "type": "topic", "title": "Public Opinion, Polling, Forecasting, and Election Data", "description": "This topic builds literacy in surveys, sampling, polling error, forecasting, turnout data, and election interpretation.", "children": [{"id": "6a7570e6-7e8c-4188-9de8-840aed0e7fa2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Polling basics", "children": [{"id": "4af8aa2e-cb79-4e91-811a-5d8f56c41b9e", "type": "concept", "title": "Sampling and weighting"}, {"id": "7597e84a-2d7e-45ab-8b0a-9001b5a60b9c", "type": "concept", "title": "Margin of error and design effects"}, {"id": "382fbeea-6d09-4faf-8f93-13b6599c9ce3", "type": "concept", "title": "Likely voter models"}], "description": "Students learn what polls can and cannot tell us."}, {"id": "59b8ff89-df66-414e-b0bc-907e8d508404", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Forecasting", "children": [{"id": "e14406fb-7f3e-4828-83f8-1db1e69df65a", "type": "concept", "title": "Polling averages"}, {"id": "c8210140-5185-4e3f-8ad9-607d8821bf5b", "type": "concept", "title": "Economic fundamentals"}, {"id": "89a8e311-f79b-42dc-8dcd-8e6cc900f4c4", "type": "concept", "title": "Probability and uncertainty communication"}], "description": "Forecasts combine polls, fundamentals, uncertainty, and assumptions."}, {"id": "23367538-440b-417f-b0fe-907370040d9d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Election data literacy", "children": [{"id": "50faeeb4-dc02-49c0-b6b5-c679d07c50b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Precinct, county, district, and national returns"}, {"id": "0492b0fe-b98b-4b3b-9c97-164fa8e86e2d", "type": "concept", "title": "Ecological inference limits"}, {"id": "3a072757-a046-49f5-9b8e-22e809f8d443", "type": "concept", "title": "Turnout, swing, and vote share"}], "description": "Students practice reading election returns responsibly."}]}, {"id": "3dab8829-7d04-4907-872b-a229ea6a33bd", "type": "topic", "title": "Campaign Strategy, Persuasion, Mobilization, and Ground Games", "description": "Students analyze how campaigns allocate scarce resources to persuade, mobilize, and communicate with voters.", "children": [{"id": "c5eacee5-70ed-44ad-93ce-2663b115b698", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Strategic environment", "children": [{"id": "bb63eab7-edc7-4cf4-9b3c-eb030566ce31", "type": "concept", "title": "Candidate quality"}, {"id": "8c2936cb-5781-4ef3-a3ab-0c3d057337d8", "type": "concept", "title": "District or state competitiveness"}, {"id": "da843d44-d012-4b38-b38b-917d22a0d94f", "type": "concept", "title": "Resources, timing, and issue agenda"}], "description": "Campaigns make choices under constraints."}, {"id": "08553fcc-d5dd-4863-8e5a-9a6401c2d49a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Persuasion and mobilization", "children": [{"id": "3aa07c2f-0f34-45f3-a9ba-705bad678e59", "type": "concept", "title": "Base mobilization"}, {"id": "4e9c8b0b-3541-47d7-819f-7ec9a470cefb", "type": "concept", "title": "Swing voter persuasion"}, {"id": "76cf2e4e-8496-42bb-9f04-4aa6e5092220", "type": "concept", "title": "Voter registration and GOTV"}], "description": "Campaigns target different voters for different purposes."}, {"id": "db84b137-78be-4276-80d6-1ec6923bd6c8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Field operations", "children": [{"id": "b5070f66-5cd1-4ef1-8d7e-8ecca8d4692d", "type": "concept", "title": "Canvassing and phone banking"}, {"id": "5a747117-6127-441a-94b5-7f2d9d72c29b", "type": "concept", "title": "Relational organizing"}, {"id": "d5d0f54e-37d2-49d8-9691-5653e37c7ca3", "type": "concept", "title": "Volunteer management and turnout tracking"}], "description": "Ground games turn strategy into contact."}]}, {"id": "dd754602-83eb-4be4-ae95-29d29d1cc566", "type": "topic", "title": "Media, Political Communication, Misinformation, and Digital Campaigning", "description": "This topic examines how information environments shape campaigns, opinion, polarization, and democratic accountability.", "children": [{"id": "02c2653c-f747-4d84-8bd1-f569b130457a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Media effects", "children": [{"id": "fef6a1d3-3882-4a9e-b93d-445c9930548c", "type": "concept", "title": "Agenda setting"}, {"id": "04031e6d-6c0d-4018-8fd9-bb5b020cf9e4", "type": "concept", "title": "Framing and priming"}, {"id": "09a5203f-88cf-41c2-b4e6-b762a4bef052", "type": "concept", "title": "Selective exposure"}], "description": "Media shapes what voters know, notice, and prioritize."}, {"id": "ff194d0b-3c27-4a73-8132-1e13d0bf0a1d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Campaign messaging", "children": [{"id": "17f526ba-811c-477d-87af-63c8fb2edc44", "type": "concept", "title": "Speeches and debates"}, {"id": "1bded4fa-8fde-4aca-8e26-15d46c583cc4", "type": "concept", "title": "Advertising and narratives"}, {"id": "2ec69ed5-2a57-43b9-b97b-061db4be6b56", "type": "concept", "title": "Issue ownership and valence appeals"}], "description": "Messages translate strategy into voter-facing communication."}, {"id": "9cb0db31-973e-4ecc-b2c2-a4627e748f88", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digital politics", "children": [{"id": "158050f7-5508-4f64-b6e0-4e142ad19474", "type": "concept", "title": "Microtargeting"}, {"id": "0a868ae0-941a-4ce9-ab8b-788c752a05b2", "type": "concept", "title": "Social media platforms"}, {"id": "b2631ddc-3560-45b2-89eb-b3d1ab80c6f3", "type": "concept", "title": "Disinformation, misinformation, and content moderation"}], "description": "Digital tools enable targeting and misinformation risk."}]}, {"id": "5b0a8857-27cb-4cb6-9adc-e9eeb5e78a11", "type": "topic", "title": "Campaign Finance, Interest Groups, and Political Influence", "description": "Students learn how money enters elections, what rules govern it, and how finance affects access, competition, and representation.", "children": [{"id": "21fe37f1-f230-48af-9c53-cffad37a12ce", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Campaign finance rules", "children": [{"id": "54e5ca43-01d1-41a6-a7c0-54ecae44dd32", "type": "concept", "title": "Contributions and expenditures"}, {"id": "95c325c7-87b1-4b98-a646-b7d755b51f43", "type": "concept", "title": "PACs and super PACs"}, {"id": "b3aaa883-2475-4d61-9c20-5e9c239e22b3", "type": "concept", "title": "Disclosure and independent expenditures"}], "description": "Students learn the basic legal architecture of election money."}, {"id": "d36385fe-6286-4be5-8fb2-da2874fcba0c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Money and competition", "children": [{"id": "6db643ed-3a55-4e6c-99d6-73fb495f2459", "type": "concept", "title": "Candidate fundraising"}, {"id": "ad36a317-89ae-463f-bd11-a4d0dc734289", "type": "concept", "title": "Outside spending"}, {"id": "69f44fa8-1a4d-45c5-97ac-adf88dcd2dd4", "type": "concept", "title": "Incumbency and challenger viability"}], "description": "Finance affects who can run and how campaigns compete."}, {"id": "8f3aa3fe-e69c-49e7-b52a-e1285e68459a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Influence and representation", "children": [{"id": "3c152553-d930-4cce-b4b0-365b4aafa6b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Access and agenda setting"}, {"id": "973c78f1-782c-46e7-b737-110609041955", "type": "concept", "title": "Interest-group influence"}, {"id": "d11e4f9e-4657-493f-9662-234e70d32cb8", "type": "concept", "title": "Small donors and public financing"}], "description": "The central question is whether money distorts political equality."}]}, {"id": "fe3e273a-72bb-497a-b02f-fefa19d4b356", "type": "topic", "title": "Primary Elections, Candidate Selection, and Intraparty Conflict", "description": "This module explains how parties choose nominees and how primaries shape ideology, accountability, and governing coalitions.", "children": [{"id": "0f16133e-26cf-4b3c-8ab8-ff947972d66b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Nomination systems", "children": [{"id": "57a564c7-3060-4836-b893-182ce8dbba62", "type": "concept", "title": "Open, closed, and semi-closed primaries"}, {"id": "3bac3389-6bb6-4c7a-937f-8235a7bc2f2b", "type": "concept", "title": "Caucuses"}, {"id": "1ba2cbc9-9111-491d-84e3-4056b00b1c10", "type": "concept", "title": "Delegate rules"}], "description": "Primaries allocate power between voters, activists, and party elites."}, {"id": "1ad2dd97-a2af-41a5-b8a2-1eba94219c79", "typ