ground states"}, {"id": "3a8775dc-b024-4196-98ab-1ac15866028b", "type": "concept", "title": "Popular vote and electoral vote divergence"}], "description": "The Electoral College structures presidential strategy and legitimacy debates."}, {"id": "e5083829-a569-4ff8-a9f1-a48aa452b625", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Representation and districts", "children": [{"id": "741276fe-99d6-4f49-82df-15ed82ddead9", "type": "concept", "title": "Redistricting and gerrymandering"}, {"id": "36453f1e-73b2-4c14-b838-64fcc782d518", "type": "concept", "title": "Malapportionment and Senate representation"}, {"id": "04bd588c-a241-45e6-ad18-02eebcecb458", "type": "concept", "title": "Descriptive and substantive representation"}], "description": "District rules shape who wins and whose preferences matter."}]}, {"id": "f69f53ba-ebc2-40d6-99d4-7dba6f456b7e", "type": "topic", "title": "Election Administration, Voting Rights, Turnout, and Election Integrity", "description": "This topic treats elections as administered systems involving registration, access, technology, law, trust, and verification.", "children": [{"id": "219931d4-daaf-4ae4-9c4d-f6eabf0ed58a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Election administration", "children": [{"id": "cee84a66-77ba-4d10-ad49-a78e246dd1f6", "type": "concept", "title": "Registration and voter rolls"}, {"id": "caf75c9c-6c75-46a4-8f58-819de2b6882b", "type": "concept", "title": "Ballot design and voting technology"}, {"id": "3ab6287f-3c88-4608-b611-faf1554a8533", "type": "concept", "title": "Mail, early, absentee, and Election Day voting"}], "description": "Elections are run through complex local, state, and federal systems."}, {"id": "eddbc744-656c-44ef-b2c7-415767140dd3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Voting rights and access", "children": [{"id": "fae53b5f-c913-4c77-a93d-8857ef71bf81", "type": "concept", "title": "Voting Rights Act"}, {"id": "d978a579-1837-4485-b23c-4a85d2d6764a", "type": "concept", "title": "ID laws and registration rules"}, {"id": "075d533a-70c9-4345-86c9-3ba34375b21f", "type": "concept", "title": "Language access and disability access"}], "description": "Rules can expand or restrict participation."}, {"id": "0f30c3c1-c1fd-4847-ae0e-5fc3eba419c6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Integrity and trust", "children": [{"id": "081b52b7-441f-4b49-b598-f6d3c7491fd1", "type": "concept", "title": "Audits and recounts"}, {"id": "1dac4f41-629b-4982-bee1-2e6964137bee", "type": "concept", "title": "Cybersecurity and misinformation"}, {"id": "beda920c-0a05-4b3f-a94d-31d746493907", "type": "concept", "title": "Certification and peaceful transfer of power"}], "description": "Election legitimacy depends on accuracy, transparency, and public confidence."}]}, {"id": "be9fe560-2791-4f73-b1de-4826f8ca25d8", "type": "topic", "title": "Polarization, Partisan Sorting, and Democratic Accountability", "description": "Students examine how polarization affects voters, parties, institutions, media, governance, and democratic norms.", "children": [{"id": "177ed427-f14b-4d16-898b-567ca1dff948", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mass polarization", "children": [{"id": "3649efe2-3b92-4350-95e8-03603a3d76ce", "type": "concept", "title": "Affective polarization"}, {"id": "f3fee2ab-23e4-4699-a897-1a9029efae7a", "type": "concept", "title": "Ideological sorting"}, {"id": "c8616f88-e64f-4a21-90d8-acdf5ac50467", "type": "concept", "title": "Negative partisanship"}], "description": "Voters increasingly organize social and political identity around party."}, {"id": "d0c2826e-d17f-42e4-8479-7da09e5b5e91", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Elite polarization", "children": [{"id": "a6c60175-9f17-4576-b823-42b52020a826", "type": "concept", "title": "Congressional polarization"}, {"id": "f882115d-23cb-4b72-8615-f3f40bfaf8e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Primary incentives"}, {"id": "bfd7304e-c47d-42e1-89b7-f0183c647277", "type": "concept", "title": "Party discipline"}], "description": "Officeholders and activists can polarize faster than voters."}, {"id": "6e9889d6-bbc0-49c7-a115-be09806753c8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Democratic accountability", "children": [{"id": "af0787e0-991d-4f1c-a331-fc692af96b38", "type": "concept", "title": "Motivated reasoning"}, {"id": "8c682403-7034-488d-a103-c02d76c14fd2", "type": "concept", "title": "Norm violations and accountability"}, {"id": "4f4e0b03-1923-442f-9540-1ff3607fb6c6", "type": "concept", "title": "Democratic backsliding risks"}], "description": "Polarization changes how voters punish or reward leaders."}]}, {"id": "36914bce-00a3-40a8-b48e-ea4c50de6641", "type": "topic", "title": "Comparative Electoral Systems and Multiparty Democracy", "description": "This topic compares plurality, majority, proportional, mixed, and ranked-choice systems and their effects on parties and representation.", "children": [{"id": "1a0af464-3e8c-4ac4-b30e-9d3b5fc53534", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Electoral formulas", "children": [{"id": "9f9ae62b-40b4-4a91-bcca-3da9b749558b", "type": "concept", "title": "Plurality and majority systems"}, {"id": "bce32970-d061-48de-8573-8dc551c83878", "type": "concept", "title": "Proportional representation"}, {"id": "43498942-0e41-4362-9235-5bd0bde6e069", "type": "concept", "title": "Mixed-member and ranked-choice systems"}], "description": "Rules convert votes into seats in different ways."}, {"id": "b738a886-88b7-4621-8f5a-a03db8dd2108", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Party system effects", "children": [{"id": "761059c4-1dc9-4d0e-a5a6-f64b8e36f3ae", "type": "concept", "title": "Effective number of parties"}, {"id": "e57a70aa-f522-46db-bf86-f15adf19be7c", "type": "concept", "title": "Thresholds"}, {"id": "0fd8a657-9462-4a9c-b269-b0c326c2fcbf", "type": "concept", "title": "Coalition formation"}], "description": "Electoral systems shape party number and coalition politics."}, {"id": "51927365-2730-4c8b-a08e-2bd4175377f8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Comparative representation", "children": [{"id": "201c0c4a-e62d-404c-947a-939ef8171a08", "type": "concept", "title": "Minority representation"}, {"id": "cc9cbaf1-94fa-4fd4-ba7c-9e69c2cacc88", "type": "concept", "title": "Women's representation"}, {"id": "04203016-fd3e-4967-ba59-10170d0272c6", "type": "concept", "title": "Government stability and responsiveness"}], "description": "Different systems trade off governability, proportionality, and accountability."}]}, {"id": "224f5218-cd86-4417-8fbd-573bdd82c583", "type": "topic", "title": "Elections Capstone: Data-Driven Campaign and Election Analysis", "description": "The course culminates in a professional analysis of an election using theory, data, institutions, communication, and democratic-quality criteria.", "children": [{"id": "facabcd0-8d60-45ec-beb6-aad98c01d129", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Case selection", "children": [{"id": "fbc8aa62-1304-475b-94a8-762d8aaa4d6c", "type": "concept", "title": "Presidential, congressional, state, local, or comparative election"}, {"id": "efa1aa61-1951-49df-b5d7-4cebd17962ab", "type": "concept", "title": "Competitive context"}, {"id": "63ac3159-ca6e-4344-9ecd-9dc84df06d97", "type": "concept", "title": "Historical baseline"}], "description": "Students select a real election and define an analytical question."}, {"id": "6480b351-0eb1-4ba3-9dfe-9130f23d8fdf", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Data and theory", "children": [{"id": "32fbc284-a49b-479f-8bed-25e0f2d8283c", "type": "concept", "title": "ANES or polling data"}, {"id": "525d50a4-4391-44c9-8aaa-e2742ac28efa", "type": "concept", "title": "Election returns"}, {"id": "2ad7c102-65db-46cc-839b-57db4a993a97", "type": "concept", "title": "Campaign finance, media, or turnout data"}], "description": "The capstone connects course theories to evidence."}, {"id": "738ff25b-65df-4b74-88ab-9fc11a21c238", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Professional output", "children": [{"id": "2b4f15c5-f49c-4e17-9462-5b0480bf65e4", "type": "concept", "title": "Executive summary"}, {"id": "9027ae0f-fbca-4e55-996d-aac65594ee07", "type": "concept", "title": "Visual evidence"}, {"id": "d9044d78-a3c5-4d6a-b4db-39f027e2d2a6", "type": "concept", "title": "Interpretation, uncertainty, and implications"}], "description": "The final product should look like an analyst memo."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$ppeljson$::jsonb,
